# Anonymous private-process access — v1 proposal

Status: DOING. Proposed 2026-10-05. No application, route, account, grant,
persistence, dependency or deployment change. The
[correction-1 independent review](reviews/private-process-proof-v1-2026-10-05.md#correction-1-disposition--superseding-bounded-pass)
records bounded PASS for the preserved corrected proposal. This later reference
edit is outside those reviewed bytes; integrated/founder acceptance and actual
HTTP/browser/store/socket enforcement remain required.

## Scope and recommendation

The [interface catalogue](INTERFACE_CATALOG.md#common-boundaries) and its
`process_ownership`/`process_authorization` field rows require process-scoped
visitor proof but leave its transport and lifecycle undefined. This proposal
refines that boundary for IF-CHAT-01–04, IF-BOOK-01–09 and IF-PRIVACY-01/02 under
[security feature 001](../../../specs/001-platform-security-hardening/spec.md),
[data constraints](DATA_CONTRACT.md#conversations-consent-and-handoff) and the
[governed handoff lifecycle](HANDOFF_LIFECYCLE.md). It adds no visitor account,
password, general identity directory or staff role. Staff JWT/bcrypt, Entra and
emergency-access requirements remain unchanged.

Recommend a **server-issued opaque proof for each private process**, delivered
only through an HTTPS HttpOnly cookie. The server binds its verifier to one
process family, selector, proof generation, permitted purposes/actions and
server-controlled validity. Possession proves access to that bounded process,
not a named person's identity, email ownership, consent or business completion.
Selectors and operation IDs remain public-to-the-caller references, not secrets
or alternate credentials. No cookie is minted merely by browsing public pages.

| Proof scope | What it can support after current checks | What it cannot establish |
|---|---|---|
| Chat session | That session's permitted chat/consent/handoff actions and events | Another session, durable storage without consent, staff assignment, live acceptance or media permission |
| Booking lineage | That lineage's qualification and permitted status/actions | Verified email, eligible slot, provider confirmation or another lineage |
| Privacy request | That verified request's minimal safe status | Authority over every record with the same email, deletion of unmapped classes or verified provider/backup removal |

Handoff remains a child of the authorized chat context, not a new transferable
visitor identity. Creating a booking from chat requires an explicit user action
and separately permitted field transfer; it does not clone the chat proof or
join histories by email. A privacy status proof is separately issued only after
the request's target scope has been verified under its approved identity policy.

## Proof and cookie representation

The proposed bearer secret contains 256 independently random bits generated by
a standard CSPRNG; use a canonical base64url representation without padding.
This proposed security margin is not a standards-mandated service limit. Generate
it independently of the process selector and operation ID; do not derive it from
email, timestamps, client input, a device fingerprint or a public digest. Store
only a nonrecoverable verifier under the separately approved cryptographic and
data-storage profile; use constant-time verification. No raw secret belongs in
database rows, replicas, jobs, evidence or telemetry. In the browser, the sole
bearer transport is the protected HttpOnly cookie specified below; do not store
the secret in script-readable storage such as localStorage/sessionStorage or
any other unapproved browser store.

Recommend `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, explicit `SameSite=Lax`, no `Domain`, `Path=/`
and an approved `__Host-` cookie name namespace. Lax supports external safe-page
navigation without permitting a state-changing GET. Prefix enforcement does not
replace attribute configuration, CSRF or object authorization. Cookies are not
isolated by port or browser tab; every application on the credential host is
inside the host trust boundary. Exact host/ingress/proxy choices remain deferred,
but untrusted applications must not share that credential boundary.

Use distinct server-controlled cookie slots for different processes and proof
generations so a late response cannot overwrite a newer credential in the same
slot. The server accepts only the current permitted generation for the selected
process; finding some other valid cookie in the request cannot authorize it.
Reject ambiguous duplicate credential names or malformed/unknown proof variants
before selecting authority; do not depend on a last-value-wins cookie parser.
Exact name syntax, encoding bounds, concurrent-process/cookie/header capacity
and safe cleanup are required transport-profile inputs before wire freeze.

Do not copy a bearer proof into JSON, a query/fragment, a WebSocket subprotocol,
localStorage/sessionStorage, a public page data block, clipboard link or an email.
Only the relevant server boundary may issue `Set-Cookie`. Private responses use
`Cache-Control: no-store`; public HTML/cache derivatives contain no per-visitor
proof, CSRF value or process data. HttpOnly prevents script reads of the cookie;
same-origin malicious scripts can still initiate actions, so it is not XSS safety.
No production attribute is relaxed to accommodate the native prototype.

## Bootstrap and uncertain creation

Recommend two closed phases at the **existing** IF-CHAT-01 or IF-BOOK-01 POST,
without a new endpoint or visible user account:

1. After an explicit Start Chat/Book action, a same-origin bootstrap request can
   allocate only a bounded ephemeral provisional context and issue its proof.
   Its response includes the nonsecret selected context and a separate CSRF
   request token, never the bearer secret. No message, email, qualification,
   consented history or external effect is admitted at this phase.
2. The actual create command supplies its scoped operation identity and CSRF
   request proof, and presents the provisional cookie. The server checks current
   provisional authority, exact closed input and permitted purpose before
   promoting that context to its single process and recording any allowed result.
   Promotion and its operation outcome use the governing process's atomic or
   reconciled authority; retries never dispatch the create again merely because
   an acknowledgement was lost. No durable personal data precedes its legal gate.

Initial bootstrap relies on exact trusted-source Origin checks and the approved
browser request/media profile because no synchronizer secret exists yet. Missing,
null, malformed or unapproved Origin denies this browser-only POST; it is not a
public safe GET, permissive form route or nonbrowser service credential. Its
allocation still needs finite abuse/work bounds. A lost bootstrap response may
leave an empty provisional context that expires under the approved policy; no
claim of exactly-once allocation follows. Cookie slots and initiating UI
generation distinguish a late bootstrap response from the chosen context.

Once the proof is issued, the selected provisional context scopes the create
operation. Changed input under the same operation conflicts. Uncertain promotion
reconciles that operation under current proof and disclosure authority, rather
than creating a new process to evade uncertainty. A context/proof alone never
proves that promotion or an external action completed. Exact bootstrap/create
envelopes, state variants, admission constraints and expiry are still required.

IF-PRIVACY-01 has different authority: verify the requested target scope using
the approved existing-process or independently reviewed subject-verification
procedure before admitting its deletion intent or issuing a request-status
proof. Knowing an email, selector or operation reference is insufficient. A
status cookie does not retrospectively verify identity or broaden deletion.
Missing identity/recovery policy leaves that affected operation unavailable.

## HTTP and WebSocket request protection

### Directional creation and admission proposal

PROPOSED refinement 2026-10-05 for the two existing POST boundaries above. Keep
the lifecycle in this document instead of introducing another creation spec.
The following names describe logical variants, not frozen JSON discriminators,
HTTP status codes or a complete schema. The current field dictionary remains
input to this refinement; unresolved identifier, consent and numeric profiles
cannot be implemented as open strings/JSON or invented defaults.

| Direction and phase | Permitted logical input/output | Excluded meaning or effect |
|---|---|---|
| Client bootstrap at IF-CHAT-01 or IF-BOOK-01 | Explicit phase selection only; the existing route supplies the process family. Origin and the reviewed media/request profile are transport checks. | No chat context/payload, email, qualification, consent decision, staff role, caller-selected proof, process identity or external action. |
| Server bootstrap response | Selected nonsecret provisional reference and separate process/generation-bound CSRF request token; bearer issuance only through the protected cookie. | Not a chat session, booking lineage, consent receipt, verified email, slot or successful promotion. No secret cookie value in JSON or echoed request. |
| Client chat create | Selected provisional reference, scoped operation identity, proposed public context `release_id`/`manifest_sha256` and optional canonical wing; only applicable closed, versioned consent decisions when offered. Cookie and CSRF proof use their separate approved transports. | Reception remains available without a wing. No initial message, history, qualification, owner/assignment, server timestamp/expiry, verified identity or provider result. Messages use the separately reviewed IF-CHAT-03 event protocol; consent changes use IF-CHAT-02 and handoff uses IF-CHAT-04. |
| Client booking-lineage create | Selected provisional reference and scoped operation identity under the current cookie/CSRF authority. | No qualification/email/consent payload, verification dispatch, slot reservation, meeting creation, marketing permission or inferred chat/history transfer. Qualification remains the six BF-01 fields plus its separate purpose-specific consent at IF-BOOK-02. |
| Server admitted result | Only the own authorized minimal session/lineage reference and creation-operation outcome, with separately permitted proof/CSRF transport. | No transcript, qualification echo, arbitrary identity, staff/queue state, email verification, slot or provider confirmation. Disclosure is rechecked before every replay. |

Chat context is an untrusted proposal: resolve the exact eligible public release,
manifest and optional wing together, and enforce withdrawal/current-source rules.
Never substitute the latest release or another wing silently under the same
operation. Consent absence/refusal preserves the eligible ephemeral path; an
unknown purpose or unacceptable notice cannot authorize persistence. No stored
notice, generic boolean or creation proof retroactively permits previous data.
Booking's initial empty context/lineage and its operation evidence must stay in
the approved bounded ephemeral path unless their own legal/data class permits
durable storage. The booking field's private-store classification is not blanket
permission to persist a visitor identifier before its policy is approved.

#### Reject before promotion; distinguish uncertainty

Admission must have a reviewed order: enforce route/method/media and finite raw
work bounds; validate the closed phase and raw representation; check exact browser
Origin, selected current proof/CSRF when required; then validate field semantics,
source/purpose eligibility and the operation's immutable meaning before effects.
Perform the applicable early origin/proof checks before costly private-data work.
Reject duplicate JSON members, malformed UTF-8, unapproved media/encoding, unknown
fields and server-owned input before promotion. Exact parser/normalization,
framing, header/body limits and status/error mapping remain transport-profile
inputs. Framework models can validate parsed fields; they cannot recover duplicate
members discarded earlier or prove current object authority.

Request-validation exceptions, logs and denial bodies must not echo raw input,
cookie/CSRF values, private object existence or another process's state. Only a
currently authorized caller may receive its bounded status/outcome. A rejection
may say no promotion was applied only when the authoritative admission path
proves that fact. A timeout, worker crash, invalid response or failed cookie write
after possible admission stays unresolved; do not manufacture a definite denial.

#### One promotion and one immutable admitted meaning

Scope operation identity by process family and selected provisional context; the
same identifier in another context cannot retrieve this result. The admitted
meaning binds the immutable allowed context and purpose/notice decisions. Exclude
transport credentials and a client clock from business meaning; rotating CSRF or
proof is not a new intent. Exact canonicalization and operation syntax remain
reviewed inputs; neither a caller digest nor JSON property order establishes
meaning or permission.

Guard the context against concurrent promotion across workers. Identical admitted
retries reconcile one operation; changed meaning conflicts. Racing different
operation IDs cannot promote the same context twice. A different ID cannot evade
pending/unknown admission or create another process after its guarded promotion.
Store/retain only the evidence permitted for that source class; a durable
idempotency table containing non-consented chat, consent refusal or raw payloads
would breach the ephemeral boundary. Missing operation evidence is not proof of
absence: consult authoritative context state, or fail unavailable without another
promotion. Expiry/restore must not forget a prior effect and reopen admission.
The physical uniqueness/transaction/fencing and expiry mechanisms remain held.

Replaying a completed operation never renews proof, consent or data retention,
reopens a closed process or repeats email/provider work. Current authority and
disclosure still govern. If promotion/rotation succeeded but its response or
new cookie was lost, the old provisional proof has no automatic continuing grant.
Reconcile only through a currently permitted proof/operation binding; otherwise
report access unavailable and use the separately approved recovery procedure.
Do not make the old credential valid again, infer access from email, cancel an
existing booking or dispatch a replacement. Exact rotation/issuance recovery
must be resolved before implementation; no universal seamless recovery is promised.

These obligations follow [HTTP retry semantics](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-9.2.2),
checked 2026-10-05: POST alone does not justify an automatic repeat after lost
acknowledgement. The per-context promotion protocol is Hengshi's proposal, not
an HTTP guarantee. Context7 `/websites/fastapi_tiangolo` and official
[FastAPI request-body guidance](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/body/)
support typed model validation, not raw-byte acceptance, privacy-safe error
projection, authorization or atomic business admission. Reuse framework primitives
only after their behavior is verified in the complete compatible stable graph.

Future public-boundary tests must cover payload smuggling at bootstrap, duplicate/
unknown/invalid raw input, unsupported consent/context, concurrent same/different
operation promotions, changed meaning, lost acknowledgement/cookie, revoked proof,
ephemeral-store loss, expiry/restore and redacted denials. No such runtime or prose
tests are run here. Exact directional schemas, transport/error variants, legal
class mappings, finite profiles, physical mechanisms, UI references and integrated/
founder acceptance remain required; no new endpoint, store, grant or account.

Recommend a server-generated synchronizer CSRF token bound to the selected
process and current proof generation. It is distinct from the HttpOnly bearer
secret, cannot grant access alone, and is delivered only by a permitted private
response. For protected HTTP mutations use the approved custom-header transport,
exact origin check and current cookie proof together. Do not accept query-token,
arbitrary form or content-type fallbacks. Public GETs require none of this;
private safe reads still require their own current process/disclosure authority.
No wildcard CORS, sibling-domain suffix match or `Origin: null` is trusted.
Target-origin/proxy trust and every direct ingress path need explicit validation.

Refresh/bootstrap information must be obtained through the existing authorized
process boundary, never an unprotected global token endpoint. Missing Origin
handling for an authorized safe read must use the reviewed request profile;
HTTP/browser contexts do not all supply identical headers. Neither SameSite,
CORS, Origin nor the CSRF token alone proves process ownership. Unknown binding
or authority denies before effects and private status/existence disclosure.

For IF-CHAT-03, verify the exact allowed browser Origin, current chat cookie,
selected session, validity and eligible context **before accepting** the
WebSocket. Browser WebSocket APIs do not offer arbitrary application headers;
the HTTP custom-header convention cannot simply be reused. Recommend a closed
first initialization frame containing the separate process-bound CSRF request
token. No private event, history, subscription or business command is delivered
or processed before that check. Initialization has a finite approved deadline,
frame/connection/work bounds and safe rejection; credentials are never echoed.

An initialized socket still requires current proof generation, consent/purpose,
process state, source eligibility and current assignment at every relevant
message, replay and outbound delivery decision. Lost authorization stops
disallowed queued delivery and closes the channel; startup checks and a periodic
timer cannot prove immediate revocation. The handoff contract's delivery/fencing
obligations govern in-flight work. IF-STAFF-15 uses separate staff identity and
assignment, never the visitor proof. Protocol/ack/replay formats and numerical
limits remain in their directional event contracts; no tutorial echo behavior,
URL token or unbounded in-memory connection manager is adopted.

## Revocation, storage and recovery

Proof validity, consent expiry, staff availability, booking challenge validity
and record retention are separate clocks. No staff 30-minute/eight-hour session
policy or visitor 90-day record rule automatically sets this proof's lifetime.
Expiry, revocation and proof-generation changes are enforced by current server
authority, not browser cookie expiry, closing a tab or deleting a local cookie.
Restored browser sessions or backups cannot resurrect a revoked proof or renew
retention. A proof missing from its authoritative store is not reconstructed from
another process, an email, cached metadata or a remembered signed cookie.

Keep non-consented chat, replay and its proof/CSRF metadata in the bounded
ephemeral path; no snapshots, persistence, logs or queue payload may silently
make that path durable. A consented process's durable records and any durable
proof/verifier require their own class-specific purpose, duration, deletion and
restore mapping. Hashes and identifiers remain linkable private metadata.
Unknown classifications or legal/store policy deny the affected persistence.
This proposal chooses no SQL columns, Redis persistence setting or retention
period and creates no visitor identity history.

Rotate/revoke proof generations when an approved authority transition requires
it, with old generations unable to authorize new data/actions or replay after
the fence. A cookie rotation response lost in transit can cause loss of access;
an unverified fallback or unlimited old-token overlap is not recovery. The
physical plan must handle issuance/promotion/rotation interleavings, lost replies,
cookie eviction and bounded cleanup. Unknown business outcomes remain intact;
loss of access cannot report cancellation, deletion, termination or confirmation.
Cross-device/email-link recovery needs a separately reviewed identity/proof
flow. No recovery secret in a URL or automatic new booking dispatch is implied.

Ending/deleting chat may invalidate its chat proof while a separately authorized
privacy request retains only its own permitted outcome projection. That status
proof does not recover deleted conversation content, extend its retention or
certify unmapped provider/backup deletion. Alias ownership remains undecided.
Proof loss explains access unavailable and keeps semantic content/Contact/Book
reachable; it does not claim a working recovery channel, owner or response SLA.

## Required implementation evidence and remaining decisions

After the applicable approvals, exercise actual HTTP, browser, store and socket
boundaries with synthetic data: wrong family/object/generation; guessed selectors;
cookie duplication/fixation; hostile/missing/null Origin; absent/mismatched CSRF;
query/body credential rejection; unknown/stale bootstrap and lost promotion;
multiple tabs and late Set-Cookie; no private disclosure before WS initialization;
revocation versus queued delivery; email correction/verification not granting
another lineage; lost/expired proof; cookie eviction; consent refusal and store
loss; deletion versus minimal status; and restore predating revocation. Check
permitted controls as well as denials. Definition examples are not runtime tests.

Before wire freeze approve the two-phase envelopes, per-family purpose/action
and identity-recovery policy, name/secret/CSRF transport profiles, cookie support
and measured capacities, exact expiry/renewal/rotation and finite work limits,
current-authorization/atomic admission and revocation fences, cryptographic
verifier handling, legal class/store/backup mappings and compatible stable graph.
Production UI references and founder acceptance remain separate. No deployment
provider, host, staff grant, legal basis or public operating claim is selected.

## Dated primary and framework observations

Checked 2026-10-05. Sources support the limited mechanics below, not acceptance
of Hengshi's two-phase/per-process design or automatic framework enforcement.

- [OWASP session guidance](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)
  recommends random server-issued secrets, one-way verifier storage and server
  expiration. Session-cookie restoration and cookie deletion do not prove
  revocation. The 256-bit margin and process binding above are this proposal.
- [Mozilla Set-Cookie reference](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Set-Cookie)
  describes Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite, host-prefix restrictions and browser cookie
  behavior; these attributes provide no object-level access decision.
- [OWASP CSRF guidance](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)
  supports synchronizer tokens for stateful applications, robust source/target
  origin validation and framework protections before custom machinery.
- [OWASP WebSocket guidance](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/WebSocket_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html)
  supports pre-upgrade origin checks, current session/message authorization and
  finite resource protection. Its example timer/size numbers are not adopted.
- Context7 `/websites/fastapi_tiangolo` and official [cookies](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/response-cookies/)
  and [WebSockets](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/websockets/) confirm
  framework cookie emission and dependency injection, not full CSRF/revocation
  enforcement. Reuse those primitives; do not copy the tutorial's query-token
  and credential-echo examples or replace accepted process authority with them.
- Official [Starlette session documentation](https://starlette.dev/middleware/)
  describes readable signed-cookie session data. It does not supply the proposed
  opaque server-state proof. The [native source observations](../../../output/research/private-process-proof-2026-10-05/native-framework-observations.json)
  identify observed prototype versions and source lines: `set_cookie` requires
  explicit Secure/HttpOnly arguments; signed session data uses base64 JSON, and
  that optional middleware cannot import here because `itsdangerous` is absent.
  No installation was attempted; neither observation selects a production version,
  CSRF middleware or complete stable graph.

## Booking creation request encoding proposal — 2026-10-06

PROPOSED encoding refinement for existing IF-BOOK-01, POST
`/api/v1/bookings/lineages`, under the directional creation/admission obligations
above. The [closed request schema](booking-creation-request.schema.json) defines
only the client body. It adds no endpoint, form, account, issued proof, storage,
calendar call or operational grant. Earlier reviewed proposal bytes remain
preserved; this refinement requires its own independent and founder acceptance.

| Phase | Exact body | Continuing authority checks |
|---|---|---|
| Bootstrap | `{ "phase": "bootstrap" }` | Explicit user initiation; exact trusted browser Origin and approved raw media/work profile. May allocate only the bounded empty ephemeral provisional context and its independently issued proof. No operation, personal/context/consent/qualification data or effects in this body. |
| Create | `{ "phase": "create", "provisional_id": "<UUID>", "operation_id": "<UUIDv4>" }` | Current selected provisional cookie and separate CSRF transport; server-allocated booking-family context, permitted empty-lineage purpose and atomic single promotion/immutable-operation reconciliation. No qualification, email, chat context, consent, slot or provider action. |

Every body is a closed object. Missing fields, unknown phases/properties, wrong
types and noncanonical UUID text reject before promotion. Do not normalize case,
trim or coerce references. Strict raw decoding still rejects duplicate members
and malformed input before schema validation; validation of a parsed object
cannot recover discarded duplicates or prove Origin/proof/CSRF authority. Keep
the existing raw JSON admission and validation-error confidentiality boundaries.
This body is not the credential transport: bearer and CSRF values are forbidden
in JSON and remain under their separately reviewed cookie/header mechanisms.

`provisional_id` adopts the common UUID representation for this one direction;
the server must resolve an allocated, current booking-family provisional context
under the exact selected proof. UUID shape, including syntactically valid Nil/Max
or a reference whose text matches the operation, proves none of those facts.
Do not rewrite other schemas or replace public release/wing identifiers.

Recommend a fresh caller-generated UUIDv4 `operation_id` from a CSPRNG for each
deliberate promotion intent, generated once and retained for authorized retry/
reconciliation. The schema narrows the common UUID shape to version 4 and its
standard variant; it cannot prove the generator's entropy or uniqueness. In a
supported secure browser, the standard `crypto.randomUUID()` is a candidate
generator. Do not substitute Math.random, timestamps, email or a device fingerprint
if unavailable; preserve truthful recovery until the authorized generator works.
This recommendation selects no package, browser matrix or database primary key.

Operation identity remains scoped to the selected provisional context and process
family. The same text in another context provides no result access; collision or
changed meaning conflicts under current authority. Proof/CSRF rotation is not new
intent, a new operation cannot evade pending promotion, and retries cannot mint
a second lineage or repeat effects. Reuse does not renew proof or retention.
Bounded operation retention/expiry, physical uniqueness/fencing, current-response
disclosure and lost-cookie recovery remain the governing lifecycle obligations.

The subsequent [booking transport/response profile proposal](#booking-creation-transport-and-response-profile-proposal--2026-10-06)
now proposes server projections, cookie/CSRF representation, lifetime/work bounds
and status/error mappings for this boundary. Acceptance and actual enforcement
remain required; this later reference is outside the request review's preserved
inputs. Chat creation keeps its distinct release/
wing and versioned consent obligations; this booking schema cannot validate it.
Qualification and purpose-specific consent remain at IF-BOOK-02. Neither bootstrap
nor create body grants durable personal storage or verifies email/booking success.

Primary guidance checked 2026-10-06: [RFC9562 UUIDv4](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-5.4)
defines its random layout; [MDN randomUUID](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Crypto/randomUUID)
documents the cryptographically secure browser generator and secure-context
requirement. Context7 `/websites/fastapi_tiangolo` was checked for request/error
handling; body-echo tutorial examples are not adopted. No framework version or
tutorial substitutes for strict decoding, confidential errors or current admission.

Focused synthetic tests exercise the actual schema/registered reference/format
validator boundary only. They prove no cryptography, browser, HTTP status/header,
cookie/CSRF, permission, transaction/concurrency, retention or operational behavior.
No documentation wording assertions or duplicate reference state machine are added.
Full wire/lifecycle definition, stable graph, independent review and integrated
Phase 1 founder approval remain required before application implementation.

Review reference added 2026-10-06: the [independent booking-request receipt](reviews/booking-creation-request-v1-2026-10-06.md)
records bounded PASS for this proposed direction and eight new plus seven common
validator tests. The [exact inspected proof bytes](../../../output/research/booking-creation-request-2026-10-06/PRIVATE_PROCESS_PROOF.md.reviewed)
remain preserved; this later reference is outside them. Shape/definition review
does not prove allocation, random generation, current admission, raw decoding,
HTTP/proof/CSRF, atomic promotion, retention or full wire/Phase 1 acceptance.

## Booking creation transport and response profile proposal — 2026-10-06

Status: DOING. This is a proposed finite profile at the existing IF-BOOK-01
`POST /api/v1/bookings/lineages`, not a new endpoint or implemented handler.
It refines the earlier directional creation and request-encoding proposals.
The unchanged [client schema](booking-creation-request.schema.json) and new
[closed server response schema](booking-creation-response.schema.json) describe
opposite directions; neither proves authorization or atomic business behavior.
This section supplies candidate transport, lifetime and work values left open
for this boundary above. Values require independent review and integrated/founder
acceptance; they are not standards-mandated defaults, measured capacity or SLAs.
Chat, privacy, qualification, email/slot/provider and staff protocols retain their
separate contracts. No local prototype attribute is relaxed or store selected.

### Same-origin request and bounded decoding

Use a browser-only, same-origin HTTPS JSON POST. Require exactly one syntactically
valid Origin whose canonical scheme/host/effective port exactly equals the trusted
public application origin configured out of band. Do not derive that trusted
origin from Host, Forwarded, X-Forwarded-* or caller input; actual trusted-proxy
binding is still an implementation/deployment input. No wildcard, suffix match,
missing/null Origin, Referer fallback or redirect to another host is admitted.
The proposed deployment keeps API and web under that credential origin; choosing
its provider/host remains D-068-deferred. Fetch uses credentials `same-origin`.

Accept `application/json` with no media parameters or only one `charset=utf-8`
parameter, case-insensitive for media/parameter syntax. Reject forms, alternate
charsets, duplicate/unknown parameters, and any Content-Encoding other than absent
or `identity`. Protocol framing must be resolved unambiguously before ASGI/body
validation; conflicting length/transfer framing cannot become ordinary JSON.
Use the shared strict UTF-8/raw JSON boundary before parsed-schema validation:
no BOM, duplicate members, trailing data, surrogate scalars, nonfinite/coerced
values or unknown properties. These particular requests contain one root object,
no arrays/nested objects and at most three members; references are canonical ASCII.

Proposed per-request maxima: 1,024 received body bytes, 16,384 aggregate decoded
header bytes including Cookie, 8,192 Cookie-value bytes across all Cookie fields,
and a five-second receive deadline. These bound streamed input as well as declared
lengths; do not trust Content-Length or join duplicate credentials away. At most
64 admitted receive/creation jobs and 1,024 allocated pre-consent contexts/operation
records exist across the service, including pending/draining work. Refuse further
admission at capacity; do not create a hidden queue or evict a live/uncertain
process to make room. Exact shared permit/store mechanisms and ingress binding
must enforce these service-wide values across workers, not multiply them per worker.
No client fingerprint, unreviewed IP retention or new per-person identity follows.
Admission/capacity checks precede allocation. Cancelling a connection cannot release
work/state before its known settlement and cleanup. These modest initial limits
must be exercised under the eventual approved graph and sized by later load tests.

Check inexpensive method/media/Origin/size gates before costly allocation; then
raw/closed shape and, for create, selected current cookie plus CSRF authority;
then allocated family/purpose, immutable operation meaning and single-promotion
authority. An already recorded matching operation is reconciled, not executed
again. A ten-second creation observation deadline may return an authorized pending
projection; it is not permission to abandon work or mark no effect. If authority
or outcome cannot be established, use a safe unavailable projection instead.

### Proof, CSRF and cookie transport

Generate bearer proof and synchronizer CSRF independently from 32 CSPRNG bytes
each. Encode each as 43 canonical unpadded base64url characters; the final character
has zero unused pad bits. Schema checks only the CSRF response representation,
not randomness or the HttpOnly cookie. The bearer verifier recommendation is
SHA-256 over the decoded random bytes with constant-time verifier comparison;
256-bit random input prevents treating this as a human-password hashing pattern.
Staff bcrypt/JWT rules are unchanged. Never emit/store/log raw bearer in JSON or
durable rows. The separate CSRF token may remain in the bounded authorized process
state for return to its current caller; exclude it from logs, caches, public HTML,
durable pre-consent storage and script-readable persistent browser storage.

Create submits the CSRF token only in a single `X-Hengshi-CSRF` request header,
with its exact canonical encoding and current process/generation binding. Require
it together with current selected cookie and exact Origin; it cannot authorize
another context, replace bearer proof or extend validity. Bootstrap does not yet
have that synchronizer token and relies on its strict Origin/media/work gates.
Do not silently accept query, body, cookie-as-CSRF or multi-valued header variants.
Keep browser CSRF state in volatile application memory scoped to the selected
process/UI generation. An explicit reload cannot recover authority from a public
page token; approved authorized recovery or Contact is required.

Proposed cookie name: `__Host-hengshi-bk-<selector32>-g<generation>`, where
selector32 is the server-issued provisional UUID rendered as its 32 lowercase
hex digits without hyphens, and generation is canonical decimal 1..9007199254740991
without leading zeros. Selectors remain nonsecret; syntactic UUIDs are not issued
authority. The server issues UUIDv4 selectors/lineages independently and guards
collisions; client UUID text alone cannot establish that generation or allocation.
Each cookie has Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, no Domain, and finite Max-Age
no larger than the remaining absolute server deadline. Server idle expiry or
revocation can end authority earlier while the cookie still exists; its presence
cannot revive that authority. An Expires value, if emitted, agrees with the
absolute cookie deadline; a negative/expired lifetime never authorizes success.

Parse original Cookie fields under the header limits. Reject duplicate recognized
Hengshi booking credential names and malformed booking namespace/name/value forms
before selecting proof; two same-name tokens never become last-value-wins.
An unselected cookie, staff token or another valid booking cannot grant this
provisional context. Admit issuance only while at most eight recognized booking
cookie slots and four current booking contexts would be present in that request's
host credential set. This is an observed-request issuance cap, not proof that an
anonymous browser with omitted cookies owns no other contexts; the service-wide
capacity bound remains necessary. Count stale booking slots until known cleanup;
refuse capacity rather than discard an active credential. Other trusted-host
cookies still count toward aggregate header limits. Exact browser coverage must
verify prefix/attribute/size behavior and graceful eviction; a prefix or nominal
browser quota cannot promise preservation. Credentials are not isolated by tab/port.

Bootstrap starts at generation 1. Atomic successful promotion rotates bearer and
CSRF to generation 2, binds current authority to the selected provisional context
and its single lineage, and invalidates generation 1 before disclosing success.
Issue the new cookie and expire the old exact slot. Late responses cannot replace
a newer generation's name; late generation-1 cookies remain invalid server-side.
Later approved rotation may advance the generation, never decrement/reuse it.
An authorized created-result replay reports the current permitted generation/CSRF,
does not issue a fresh bearer, renew a lifetime or recover a lost cookie from its
stored verifier. This section approves no later rotation or recovery endpoint.

### Server projections, status and uncertainty

| Response | HTTP | Closed projection and meaning |
|---|---:|---|
| Bootstrap ready | 200 | `phase=bootstrap`, `state=provisional`, selected `provisional_id`, `proof_generation=1`, separate `csrf_token`; protected bearer only in Set-Cookie. No lineage or booking success. |
| Created or currently authorized matching replay | 200 | `phase=create`, `state=created`, selected `provisional_id`, same `operation_id`, own `lineage_id`, current `proof_generation` at least 2 and separate current `csrf_token`. One empty BOOKING_STARTED lineage, never qualification/email/slot/provider confirmation. |
| Currently authorized unresolved operation | 202 | `phase=create`, `state=pending`, selected `provisional_id` and scoped `operation_id`; no lineage, generation, token or completed result claim. Reconcile the same intent through this existing boundary under current authority. |
| Invalid closed/raw request | 400 | `state=unavailable`, `code=INVALID_REQUEST`, `recovery=correct_request`. |
| Body/media/header rejection | 413 / 415 / 431 | Same unavailable projection with BODY_TOO_LARGE / UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA / HEADER_TOO_LARGE, each `recovery=correct_request`. Ingress may safely terminate before an application JSON body; absence of a body is no business result. |
| Missing/expired/revoked/unusable authority | 403 | ACCESS_UNAVAILABLE with `recovery=contact`; do not distinguish unknown private object from invalid current proof. |
| Currently authorized action/CSRF denial | 403 | ACTION_DENIED with `recovery=contact`; no raw value or private state echo. Without current object authority use ACCESS_UNAVAILABLE instead. |
| Authorized immutable-meaning conflict | 409 | OPERATION_CONFLICT with `recovery=reconcile`; no replacement intent/lineage or automatic retry. |
| Bounded admission exhausted | 503 | CAPACITY_LIMIT with `recovery=wait`; a previous matching operation may still exist, so this does not establish absence of earlier effects. |
| Store/worker/outcome unavailable | 503 | SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE with `recovery=reconcile`; uncertainty and no currently permitted disclosure remain authoritative. |

All projections use `Content-Type: application/json` and `Cache-Control: no-store`,
with no permissive cross-origin credential access. Produce strict UTF-8 JSON under
the response schema and matching numeric/scalar rules, not arbitrary framework
exception bodies. Error objects have only state/code/recovery: no input echo,
free-form detail, object/operation reference, private existence, staff, cookie or
CSRF. Localized explanation comes from an approved fixed code-to-copy map, not
server exception text. Bound emitted JSON to 1,024 bytes before headers; response
shape alone does not prove header/cookie or raw encoding conformity.

Unavailable describes the current safe projection, not proof that no earlier
promotion occurred. A client timeout, invalid/lost body, failed cookie acceptance
or 202 never means completion or definite noncompletion. Retain the selected intent
and reconcile only under current proof/CSRF. No unauthorized recovery by email,
selector, old generation or operation ID; no replacement that evades uncertainty.
A syntactically valid created body is used only when it matches the initiating
UI generation/context/operation and the currently authorized server result; it
does not prove the browser accepted its protected cookie. A lost rotated cookie
can leave a known created lineage inaccessible; expose truthful Contact recovery,
not a second promotion. No retry, status read or receipt refresh renews authority.

### Initial lifetimes and data-class separation

Propose an empty provisional context with a five-minute absolute server lifetime,
and initial lineage access with 30-minute idle and two-hour absolute lifetimes
measured from successful promotion. Only an explicitly admitted permitted user
business action can reset idle time, within the absolute limit; background polls,
CSRF reads, duplicate create/replay, failures and transport heartbeats cannot.
CSRF is valid only while its bound current proof generation is valid, not under a
longer independent deadline. Cookie Max-Age is a transport hint capped to the
absolute server deadline; idle/revocation checks remain separate current authority.
Keeping a cookie for that absolute interval allows permitted idle renewal without
reissuing a bearer on a replay, but never bypasses an already expired idle deadline. Cookie deletion or tab closure is
neither verified record deletion nor a cancellation of a booking/provider action.

Before purpose-specific consent/legal storage permission, provisional references,
empty lineage, proof/CSRF and operation evidence remain in the approved bounded
ephemeral path; no transcript, qualification, email, IP profile or hidden durable
idempotency record is added. A lost ephemeral store cannot reconstruct them from
backups/logs or accept the forgotten selector as fresh. Expiry never reopens a
previously promoted context. Pending/draining authority keeps its reservation and
single-promotion fence until settlement/cleanup is known; capacity pressure or a
five-minute timer does not erase an uncertain effect. Admission fails unavailable
when the necessary evidence is absent. Actual uniqueness/fencing, permitted store
class and restore behavior must enforce this, not rely on schema or cache TTL.

Access lifetime is separate from retention. Existing purpose-specific consent,
90-day chat/brief/lead policy and approved active-client/legal exceptions govern
their classes; this profile creates no new retention basis or deletion deadline.
Later qualification, verified-email recovery, provider retries, reschedule/cancel
and privacy identity remain their own contracts. Public alias ownership stays
undecided; Contact recovery describes a route, not monitored mailbox or response SLA.

### Primary support and acceptance boundary

Checked 2026-10-06: Context7 `/websites/fastapi_tiangolo` and official
[FastAPI cookies](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/response-cookies/) explain
cookie/header emission alongside response filtering, and direct responses' filtering
responsibility. They provide primitives, not automatic CSRF, proof/replay or raw
JSON enforcement. Exact installed behavior needs the complete compatible graph.
[MDN Set-Cookie](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Set-Cookie)
explains host-prefix/attribute requirements, forbidden script access and cookie
expiry. [RFC 6265 section 6.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6265.html#section-6.1)
describes general user-agent capacity guidance and eviction, not guaranteed slots.
[OWASP CSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)
supports a bound synchronizer token, separate transport and trusted origin checks;
[OWASP sessions](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)
supports server-side expiry and independent idle/absolute controls.
[RFC 9110](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-15.3.3)
distinguishes accepted from completed work. These sources do not mandate this
proposal's names, exact numeric lifetimes/caps or two-phase promotion protocol.

Independent review and integrated/founder acceptance remain. Actual handler/raw
parser/ingress, cookie/Origin/CSRF, distributed work/fencing/store, lifetime/restore,
privacy-safe errors, same/different-operation races, lost acknowledgements/cookies,
browser and measured load tests must prove their respective obligations after
implementation authorization. Schema fixtures establish representation only.
No new account, grant, persisted data, production UI, cloud/provider choice,
dependency, application code, runtime security or complete Phase 1 approval follows.

Review reference added 2026-10-06: [booking creation profile review PASS](reviews/booking-creation-http-v1-2026-10-06.md)
covers the exact appended profile, response schema and actual validator boundary
at frozen inputs. Eight response, eight request and seven common-value methods
pass independently. The [inspected proof document](../../../output/research/booking-creation-http-2026-10-06/PRIVATE_PROCESS_PROOF.md.reviewed)
is preserved; this reference reconciliation is outside those bytes. Numerical
capacities/lifetimes remain unmeasured proposals. No actual HTTP/cookie/CSRF,
distributed fencing/store/expiry/recovery, full graph or founder approval follows.

## Chat creation request encoding proposal — 2026-10-06

PROPOSED refinement of existing IF-CHAT-01, POST `/api/v1/chat/sessions`.
The [closed client schema](chat-creation-request.schema.json) covers both
creation phases; it adds no endpoint, conversation store or permission. Earlier
reviewed bytes remain preserved. This additive shape needs independent review
and integrated/founder acceptance before wire freeze or implementation.

| Phase | Body | Continuing admission |
|---|---|---|
| Bootstrap | `{ "phase": "bootstrap" }` only | Deliberate initiation, trusted Origin and bounded raw request; allocate only an empty chat-family provisional context. No release, message, consent or identity payload. |
| Create | `phase`, `provisional_id`, `operation_id`, `context`; optional `consent` | Current selected chat proof and separate CSRF, exact release/checksum/wing eligibility, approved purpose/notice rules and atomic single promotion with immutable scoped operation meaning. |

Use the existing common lowercase UUID for the provisional selector and the
existing caller UUIDv4 operation representation; neither is a credential.
The operation remains scoped to this chat provisional context, not the booking
family whose representation is reused. `context` requires `release_id` and
`manifest_sha256` using publication representations. Its optional `wing_key`
selects only one of the five canonical service wings. Omit it for Reception;
null, an invented department or an inferred hidden route is not absence.
Resolve the exact eligible context together; never silently substitute another
release, checksum or wing. The request contains no initial message/history,
qualification, staff assignment, server timestamp or provider outcome.

An omitted `consent` means no grant and retains eligible ephemeral guidance.
When offered, `consent.decisions` is a nonempty array of closed records:
`purpose_key`, `notice_reference` and `decision` (`grant` or `refuse`). Each
notice reference contains `notice_id`, `notice_revision` and `notice_sha256`.
These bounded identifier/hash representations propose an exact immutable notice
binding; they do not create notice text, legal purpose keys or approved policy.
Before accepting any decision, resolve the purpose and exact immutable notice
under the currently approved offer and policy. Never accept caller notice copy,
a generic boolean, arbitrary invented keys or a grant inferred from creation.
Unknown/unmapped purposes or unacceptable notices cannot grant persistence;
deny that malformed decision set before promotion rather than silently changing
its meaning. The visitor may deliberately retry an eligible ephemeral creation
with a new operation intent and no consent; do not auto-rewrite the failed intent.
Recognized refusal preserves eligible ephemeral guidance and grants no other
purpose. A grant alone cannot enable storage while its legal/store/restore
mapping is held, nor authorize handoff, marketing, booking or prior data.

The proposed shape cap is eight decisions, unmeasured and subject to the common
private raw JSON profile and stricter eventual route admission. `uniqueItems`
rejects identical records only. Semantic admission must also reject repeated
purpose keys even with different notices or grant/refuse values. Never choose
the last duplicate, merge conflicting choices or treat array order as priority.
Bind the immutable operation to context and an order-independent validated
purpose/notice/decision map. The same map may reconcile under the same operation;
changed context or any changed decision conflicts. Proof/CSRF rotation and client
clocks are not business meaning. Current authority is checked on every replay.

Consent changes remain IF-CHAT-02; messages/replay IF-CHAT-03 and handoff IF-CHAT-04.
No consent-store durability, response shape, HTTP/work/lifetime profile or socket
protocol is selected by this request schema. Complete those separate directional
contracts, policy registrations and measured bounds before wire freeze.
Strict UTF-8/duplicate-member/number admission precedes parsed-object validation.
Schema fixtures test representation only, never notice legitimacy, release
eligibility, proof/CSRF, concurrency, persistence or actual request enforcement.

Dated 2026-10-06: official [object](https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/reference/object)
and [array](https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/reference/array)
references explain required/closed properties and whole-item uniqueness. They
do not provide Hengshi consent policy or property-key uniqueness enforcement.

Review reference added 2026-10-06: [chat creation request review PASS](reviews/chat-creation-request-v1-2026-10-06.md)
covers only this appended encoding, closed schema and actual validator tests.
The [inspected proof bytes](../../../output/research/chat-creation-request-2026-10-06/snapshots/05-PRIVATE_PROCESS_PROOF.md)
remain frozen; this reference addition is outside them. Purpose/notice policy,
response/transport/lifetime/socket contracts, actual admission/consent enforcement,
the complete stable graph and integrated/founder acceptance remain held.

## Chat creation HTTP, consent projection and lifetime proposal — 2026-10-06

PROPOSED refinement at existing IF-CHAT-01. The request schema above and
[closed response schema](chat-creation-response.schema.json) remain opposite
directions, not authorization or runtime evidence. The numerical values below
are initial engineering proposals, unmeasured and awaiting independent/integrated
and founder acceptance. They do not adopt booking authority, staff lifetimes,
legal storage permission, provider behavior or a deployment provider.

### Request admission, response encoding and finite creation work

Use browser-only same-origin HTTPS POST and the exact trusted Origin,
media/charset/content-encoding, original-header parsing, no redirects/permissive
CORS and privacy-safe error rules of the booking creation transport section.
Apply the common private raw JSON profile before parsed-object/schema validation.
Do not inherit booking's no-array/no-nesting request description or 1,024-byte
body/response sizes: chat's context and optional decision/notice records are
nested. Proposed received body and emitted response maxima are each 8,192 bytes,
still subject to the common stricter scalar/name/depth/number limits. Retain the
16,384-byte aggregate header ceiling, 8,192-byte combined Cookie-value ceiling
and five-second receive deadline. Bound streamed/declared input before allocation
and emitted encoded bytes before headers; no unbounded framework parser or error
echo is permitted. Multiple messages, transcript or provider output are excluded.

Add a jointly enforced outer creation ceiling of 64 admitted receive/creation
jobs and 1,024 allocated provisional/process-operation contexts for chat plus
booking, including pending/draining reservations. Each family also retains its
own applicable limit; the new shared ceiling cannot enlarge booking's earlier
profile. This is an explicit proposed cross-family admission refinement, not a
claim that an existing counter already covers chat. Creation budgets do not
replace separately bounded active sockets, messages, replay or provider work.
One service-wide coordinator must enforce the ceiling across workers; starting
another worker, losing a connection or reaching a timer cannot free an unsettled
reservation. Do not allocate a hidden queue, evict a live context or fingerprint
visitors to enforce it. Store/clock/capacity uncertainty denies new admission.

After cheap route/media/Origin/size gates, strictly decode the closed request.
Create additionally requires the current selected chat proof and CSRF before
private lookup. Resolve its family/context and scoped operation. A known same
operation compares its original immutable context/decision map and reconciles;
it never reapplies an old grant. Current disclosure/source/consent authority is
still checked. Only a new promotion evaluates the currently offered notice and
purpose eligibility and atomically admits that meaning. Unknown/changed meaning
cannot become another session, silent context substitution or auto-corrected
consent. If ten seconds elapse observing an admitted promotion, an authorized
pending projection may be returned while work/reservation/fences remain held.
This observation deadline neither cancels effects nor proves noncompletion.

### Chat-specific proof and cookie family

Independently generate 32-byte CSPRNG bearer and synchronizer CSRF tokens with
the canonical 43-character base64url representation, one-way bearer-verifier
storage/constant-time comparison and volatile CSRF handling described above.
Representation reuse does not reuse a booking secret, selector, verifier or
purpose. The proposed chat name is
`__Host-hengshi-ch-<selector32>-g<generation>` using its independently server-issued
provisional UUID's lowercase unhyphenated digits and canonical safe-integer
generation. Session UUIDs are independently issued with collision guards.
Use Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, no Domain, with finite Max-Age capped
to remaining absolute server validity. Its cookie is the bearer; only the separate
current `X-Hengshi-CSRF` header and exact Origin complete create authorization.
Reject duplicate/malformed recognized chat names/values before selecting a proof;
no query/body token, booking/staff credential or last-value-wins parser fallback.

At issuance, propose at most eight recognized chat cookie slots and four current
chat contexts observed in that request's host credential set, with stale slots
counted until known cleanup. Booking caps remain separate; all cookies contribute
to the shared header ceiling. Omitted cookies do not prove anonymous ownership
of no other processes, so the joint service-wide ceiling is still required.
Do not discard an active credential to admit another. Browser eviction/support
must be measured; cookies are not isolated by tab or port.

Bootstrap begins at generation 1. Successful single promotion binds the one
session, rotates bearer/CSRF to generation 2 and invalidates generation 1 before
disclosing the created projection. Issue the new named slot and expire the old
exact slot. Late old-generation replies cannot overwrite a newer generation's
name or grant access. A currently authorized replay reports only current allowed
generation/CSRF and consent projection; it never issues a replacement bearer or
renews validity. Loss of the rotated cookie is access loss, not proof of failed
promotion and not authority to recover by session ID, operation ID or email.

### Truthful server and consent projections

| HTTP / state | Closed projection and meaning |
|---|---|
| 200 / provisional | Same represented bootstrap fields as booking, resolved exclusively under the chat route/family: provisional selector, generation 1 and separate CSRF. No session, message or consent receipt. |
| 200 / created | `phase=create`, `state=created`, selected provisional/operation, own `session_id`, current generation at least 2, separate CSRF and the current `consent` projection below. No transcript, staff assignment or AI/provider answer. |
| 202 / pending | Selected provisional/operation only; no session, generation, token or consent receipt. Acknowledge uncertainty and reconcile the same intent through IF-CHAT-01 under current proof. |
| Safe unavailable error | Reuse only booking's closed code/recovery pairs and their HTTP mappings. ACTION_DENIED may cover a currently authorized but inadmissible purpose/notice set; lack of object authority uses ACCESS_UNAVAILABLE. No private selector, echo or free-form policy detail. |

Response representation reuse supplies no booking lineage, qualification or
calendar effect. Return `application/json`, `Cache-Control: no-store` and strict
UTF-8 under the schema/raw profile and output-byte cap. An unavailable projection
cannot assert no prior effect. Match successful replies to the current initiating
UI generation/provisional/operation; body shape never proves cookie acceptance.
No raw bearer, transcript, contact details or provider result is returned.

`consent={state:none}` means this session has no applied purpose decisions and
therefore no inferred grant; eligible guidance stays ephemeral. The alternative
is `{state:current, revision:<positive exact integer>, decisions:[...]}`: the
server's current approved purpose-specific decision map using the request's
closed immutable-notice representation. This is not a boolean storage mode or
permission bundle. Recognized refusal may have a current ephemeral receipt; a
receipt's existence does not grant durable consent-proof retention. Only current
registered purposes/notices and actually applied scoped decisions may appear.
No repeated purpose keys, future notice, client timestamp or invented effective
grant. A grant is admitted/applied only after its specific legal/store/restore
mapping and offered notice are approved; missing mapping denies that decision set
before promotion. It does not auto-dispatch handoff, marketing, booking or model
work, nor authorize pre-consent data. Omission or an explicitly recognized refusal
still permits the eligible ephemeral path without those grants.

The revision is server-owned, initially 1 when the first decision map is actually
applied, then monotonically advanced by separately guarded IF-CHAT-02 transitions.
No map means no invented revision. Replaying creation after a later withdrawal
must not replay its historical grant: under current authority, report the current
permitted revision/decisions or a safe unavailable result. Do not rewrite the
original operation meaning or recreate a withdrawn consent record. The client
fences older consent projections by revision and selected UI/proof generation;
none/creation responses cannot overwrite a later authoritative consent revision.
Exact IF-CHAT-02 acknowledgements and IF-CHAT-03 initialization/events still need
their own directional contracts and concurrency tests. Consent changes fence
disallowed writes/output even while base session proof remains valid.

### Access lifetime, retention and pending cleanup

Independently propose chat provisional validity of five minutes absolute and
created chat access of 30 minutes idle/two hours absolute from successful
promotion. These happen to match the initial booking numbers but are separate
chat clocks, not inherited ownership or an approved SLA. Only a deliberately
admitted permitted user business action may refresh idle within absolute expiry.
Creation replay, polling, CSRF reads, provider replies, socket heartbeats,
reconnection and failures cannot. CSRF ends with its bound current proof; current
source, consent, withdrawal and authorization can deny earlier. Clock uncertainty
cannot extend an expiry; shared time/fencing must be specified and measured.

Session access expiry is separate from approved consented-record retention and
the held 90-day policy anchor/class mappings. It permits no blanket deletion or
keepalive. Ephemeral process/message/replay/proof state has no snapshots, durable
logs or recovery from PostgreSQL. When lost, deny access rather than reconstruct
it from a remembered selector. An expired provisional cannot reopen after a
possibly admitted promotion; pending/draining reservations and single-promotion
evidence remain until known settlement and approved cleanup. No timer or lost
connection manufactures cancellation, erases uncertainty or releases capacity.
A new deliberately initiated session is not recovery of an old session/transcript
and cannot overwrite its unresolved outcome. Durable grants and consent-proof
retention remain unavailable until their exact policy/store/deletion/restore
mapping is approved. Public alias ownership remains undecided; Contact/Book
recovery describes semantic routes, not a monitored mailbox or response SLA.

Checked 2026-10-06: Context7 `/websites/fastapi_tiangolo` and official
[FastAPI cookie guidance](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/response-cookies/)
confirm explicit cookie/header emission and direct-response filtering obligations,
not session/CSRF enforcement. [MDN Set-Cookie](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Set-Cookie)
documents cookie transport/prefix behavior; [OWASP sessions](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)
supports server-controlled idle/absolute expiry and privilege-transition renewal;
[RFC 9110](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-15.3.3) distinguishes
accepted from completed work. None mandates these particular numeric proposals.

Before implementation, independently review/accept this encoding and profile,
register policy/origin/clock/store/graph mechanisms, then exercise actual raw HTTP,
cookies/CSRF, shared work limits, races/lost replies/late generations, current
consent, expiry/replay/store loss and denial paths. Schema fixtures prove shape
only. Socket/AI/handoff protocols, production screens, provider capabilities,
privacy/legal binding, full Phase 1 acceptance and implementation remain held.

## Chat consent changes and acknowledgements proposal — 2026-10-06

Status: DOING, unreviewed. Refine existing IF-CHAT-02 only:
`PATCH /api/v1/chat/sessions/{session_id}/consent`. This is a directional
definition, not a handler, legal approval, completed deletion or storage grant.
The catalogue's versioned purpose-specific change and effective-state rows,
DATA-005/006 and the governed handoff withdrawal rules remain controlling.

### Request and authority

Propose one closed JSON object with `operation_id` and `consent`. The operation
uses the existing UUIDv4 representation, scoped to this session and IF-CHAT-02;
it cannot reuse creation, booking or handoff authority. `consent` contains only
`expected_revision` and `decisions`. The expected revision is an exact positive
binary64-safe integer for an existing decision map. For the first map only,
explicit JSON null means the caller observed no map; it matches only actual
absence, never a withdrawn map, expired context or missing store. This refines
the field catalogue's positive-integer case for changing an existing record.
Zero, omission, numeric strings and client timestamps are not substitutes.

There are one to eight decisions with distinct approved `purpose_key` values:

| Client decision | Required fields / admission |
|---|---|
| `grant` or `refuse` | `purpose_key`, `decision`, and the existing closed immutable `notice_reference`. Verify the offered purpose, exact presented notice and current applicable policy before applying the complete set. Grant also requires its approved storage/transfer/provider mapping. |
| `withdraw` | Only `purpose_key` and `decision`. Resolve the previously admitted purpose under current own-process authority. No acceptance of a new notice, new grant or email verification is required to withdraw it. A retired notice cannot prevent revocation of its existing grant. |

Reject extra fields, duplicate purpose keys (including differing notices), unknown
purposes and invalid combinations before applying any change. Never replace the
whole map from client input: only named purposes change; omitted purposes retain
their current state. Grant/refusal notices cannot authorize earlier ephemeral
content retroactively. Refusal leaves eligible ephemeral guidance available.

Use the creation proposal's raw JSON/UTF-8, media, body/header/cookie limits and
same-origin HTTPS protections, with PATCH rather than POST. Check allowed Origin,
current chat cookie/generation, selected session, validity and bound CSRF before
private lookup, outcome disclosure or mutation. Staff identity is not a substitute
for visitor consent. There is no proof/CSRF input in this JSON and no secret echo.

### Atomic change, withdrawal and retries

Serialize admission against current authority, expected map revision and the
scoped operation. Apply the entire decision set atomically. A new accepted intent
advances the server revision exactly once, including an explicit refusal or
withdrawal whose effective permission was already absent. Keep that revision
after the last grant is withdrawn; do not reset to null or reuse an old revision.
At the exact-integer ceiling, deny new changes rather than wrap the revision.
Two intents against the same revision cannot both win. A stale intent returns
conflict, never an automatic merge, rebase or silently updated expected revision.

Withdrawal makes that purpose ineligible at the guarded authority boundary.
Before acknowledging it as applied, fence new persistence/transfer and stale
worker/socket output dependent on that purpose. Unknown fencing fails closed and
cannot produce an applied acknowledgement. Existing bytes already delivered are
not retractable. Terminate/disallow affected ongoing handoff or media actions
under their separate contracts; do not claim a remote provider has erased data.
Start the mapped deletion workflow for existing retained classes without treating
that workflow's completion as part of this acknowledgement. Required legal proof,
audit/suppression, backups and provider deletion have separate held mappings.

Same-operation/same-intent retries reconcile under current proof and authority;
they do not apply the decisions again. Different content under that identity is
an operation conflict. A known historical grant is never replayed into authority
after a withdrawal. If the original outcome is known, return its application
revision together with the current safe effective map, not its old grant map.
If operation evidence is no longer available, deny/reconcile safely rather than
infer that the intent did not run. The current revision guard still prevents an
old intent from being admitted again; state loss cannot reconstruct authority.

### Response and finite work

| HTTP / state | Proposed closed projection and meaning |
|---|---|
| 200 / `applied` | `state`, selected `operation_id`, server `applied_revision`, current `proof_generation` and `consent.effective_state`. The effective state contains current `revision` and purpose decisions (`grant`, `refuse`, `withdrawn`); grant/refusal includes its immutable notice reference, withdrawal does not require a new notice. No history, bearer, assignment, provider result, expiry or deletion-completion field. |
| 202 / `pending` | Only `state` and selected `operation_id`, after own-process checks. Outcome/fencing is unresolved. No effective grant, application revision or success assertion. Reconcile the same intent. |
| 409 / unavailable | Minimal fixed operation/stale conflict and reconcile recovery, only after authorization. Never echo private fields or offer silent resubmission with a newer revision. |
| Other denial / unavailable | Use the creation profile's minimal fixed transport/access/capacity/service error projections and statuses; do not reveal whether another session exists. |

The creation endpoint's existing grant/refuse projection is unchanged. After a
withdrawal, creation replay must not invent a new refusal notice or replay an old
grant; where its projection cannot express the current permitted state faithfully,
return its existing safe unavailable result. IF-CHAT-02's current projection is
the proposed consent recovery representation, not permission to add a public GET.
All responses are no-store. The client fences by selected session, proof
generation and current consent revision; an older response cannot restore a grant.

Propose a separate shared consent-work pool of 64 admitted jobs, at most one
in-flight mutation per existing context, with no hidden queue. Within the existing
finite context allocation, retain at most the current pending intent and latest
terminal outcome per context; do not retain unbounded operation history. These
are unmeasured proposal limits, not approved capacity or a production mechanism.
An unresolved job retains its reservation until known settlement; a timeout or
disconnect does not cancel it or prove no effect. Reject new work on capacity or
store uncertainty. Uncertain permission denies dependent output/actions while
reconciliation is pending. No heartbeat, retry or status response renews access;
only an admitted deliberate permitted user change may refresh idle within the
existing absolute limit. No raw payload/notice/operation log creates unapproved
durable refusal, consent-proof or non-consented transcript storage.

### Source, review and implementation obligations

[RFC 5789 §2](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5789.html#section-2) requires atomic
PATCH application and explains collision protection; this application's body
revision guard is not a claim to implement HTTP If-Match. [RFC 9110 §15.3.3](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-15.3.3)
distinguishes accepted work from completion. [OWASP authorization](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)
and [CSRF guidance](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)
support current permission and CSRF checks; they do not prescribe these counts or
legal consent semantics. Context7 `/websites/fastapi_tiangolo` and [FastAPI error
handling](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/) were checked on
2026-10-06: exception/validation handlers are available, but default diagnostic
detail/body examples are not this profile's private error projection.

Independent security/architecture review remains required; no verdict exists.
Before implementation, freeze directional schemas and approved legal/purpose/
notice/retention mappings, specify atomic store/fencing and measured resource
mechanisms, then test actual HTTP/store/socket boundaries: cross-process/CSRF
denial, absent-map versus withdrawn revision, duplicate keys, partial-set failure,
stale concurrent grants, withdraw versus in-flight output, lost reply/replay after
withdrawal, uncertain commit/capacity, notice retirement and expiry/state loss.
No ordinary prose test or schema fixture can prove those runtime behaviors.
IF-CHAT-03 events and downstream acknowledgement/deletion contracts remain held.

The subsequent proposed [directional schema module](chat-consent.schema.json)
encodes these request/response shapes through explicit `$defs/request` and
`$defs/response`; its root rejects instances. It remains unreviewed. Unique
purpose keys, current revision/notice authority, application-to-effective revision
ordering, atomic withdrawal/fencing and HTTP status are semantic/runtime checks,
not schema guarantees. This navigation addition is outside the first frozen
directional-proposal review packet; the prior proposal bytes are retained there.
The resulting effective map is bounded to eight purpose entries, including
withdrawn entries, matching the creation projection's existing bound. Check that
result before atomic application; no silent eviction/reset of withdrawal state.
The limit is proposed and unmeasured, not a standards-mandated policy count.

### Current creation/consent review disposition — 2026-10-06

The [joint independent review](reviews/chat-creation-consent-v1-2026-10-06.md)
records bounded PASS for the exact creation response/HTTP/lifetime and consent
proposal/schema/test inputs. Its 27 frozen identities and 15 independently
reproduced schema methods establish definition coherence and representation only.
Earlier unreviewed/terminated-review notices in these dated proposal sections
are superseded for the receipt's exact scope; historical packets remain intact.
This later reference addition is outside the inspected bytes. It changes no
protocol, limit, policy, authorization, lifecycle or field. Numerical targets,
legal/store/clock/fencing mechanisms, production UI, actual HTTP/store/socket
enforcement, stable compatibility and integrated/founder acceptance remain held.

## Booking status read and client ordering proposal — 2026-10-07

Status: DOING. This refines existing IF-BOOK-07, GET
`/api/v1/bookings/lineages/{lineage_id}`, under ACT-29 and BF-01. It is a proposed
read protocol, not a new endpoint, visitor account, cancellation entitlement,
wire-format freeze or application implementation. IF-BOOK-08/09 remain separately
gated by approved ownership, cutoff/lifetime and provider rules. The existing
[field dictionary](process-fields.csv), [booking lifecycle](INTERFACE_CATALOG.md#booking-lineage-and-external-effect)
and BF-01 own process meaning; no additional qualification question is introduced.

### Current authorized observation, without a new effect

The path is only an untrusted canonical lineage selector. Validate the current
booking-family proof, generation, expiry/revocation and exact lineage binding
against authoritative state before reading or disclosing private status. A saved
UUID, cached response, verified email fact, valid chat proof or staff identity
alone cannot authorize this visitor read. Missing/unknown proof-store state is not
reconstructed from a browser cookie or another family. Apply current disclosure
and data-class constraints again at the response boundary; an earlier read grant
cannot survive a revocation fence. The implementation must define that boundary's
ordering against concurrent withdrawal/revocation before claiming enforcement.

Proposed browser transport is same-origin HTTPS fetch with same-origin credentials,
no redirect following, no request body or query parameters, and JSON response
negotiation. Use the selected current booking cookie, never a URL/body bearer or
caller-selected generation. No proof rotation, bootstrap or synchronizer-token
issuance occurs at this GET. The state-changing Origin/CSRF profile continues to
control mutations; it is not copied into a read that normal browser contexts may
send without Origin. A present Origin must match the trusted origin exactly; null,
malformed or foreign values deny. A missing Origin is not ownership evidence:
current proof/disclosure checks and the explicitly restricted same-origin response
policy still apply. No cross-origin CORS grant, JSONP, HTML/script response or
redirect-to-login/provider is introduced. Native-browser/header/ingress behavior
and response isolation need their own implementation qualification.

Reading status cannot create or promote a lineage, verify email, select/reserve a
slot, submit/retry an external operation, enqueue provider reconciliation, schedule
an alert, reschedule/cancel, extend access/retention or mark an old intent successful.
Reconciliation is independently admitted work under the existing authorized owner;
GET observes its committed result. A user refresh, background poll, repeated GET,
conditional request or retry after a network error is not a new business intent.
Any permitted diagnostics remain minimal and cannot log the private selector,
qualification, bearer, challenge or meeting payload. Exact finite request/work and
refresh-rate limits remain qualification inputs; no unrestricted polling is approved.

### Snapshot meaning and HTTP association

Construct one coherent, currently authorized snapshot from the booking authority.
Return the own lineage ID, its committed revision and exact accepted BF-01 state;
do not combine a state from one revision with occurrence data from another. The
revision uses the existing common positive-revision proposal and tracks actual
guarded changes, not fetches, browser clocks or an independently refreshed provider
panel. The minimal safe occurrence projection remains a separate closed-format
input; this section does not invent timestamps, meeting URLs or provider IDs.

| Observed state | Permitted meaning |
|---|---|
| BOOKING_STARTED, VALIDATION_ERROR, QUALIFICATION_COMPLETE, EMAIL_PENDING, EMAIL_EXPIRED, EMAIL_UNDELIVERABLE, VERIFIED, NO_AVAILABILITY, SLOT_SELECTED | Exactly that accepted step/branch. VERIFIED is email ownership only; a selected slot is not a booking or reservation guarantee. |
| BOOKING_PENDING, RECONCILIATION_ERROR | Local pending/uncertain state. No guessed failure or confirmed occurrence from a provider timeout, alert, optimistic client or calendar screenshot. |
| CONFIRMED_QUALIFIED | Only the committed result of the required matching local and approved calendar/meeting reconciliation. No attendance, future availability or response-time promise. |
| RESCHEDULE_PENDING, CANCEL_PENDING | The requested change is unresolved. Any permitted old occurrence is explicitly the last reconciled truth, not proof the external state remains unchanged or that a replacement/cancellation succeeded. |
| CANCELLED | Only the committed reconciled cancellation result. It does not mean record deletion, retention expiry, terminated chat or withdrawn consent. |

Proposed HTTP mapping: 200 means this authorized status representation was read,
even when its booking state is pending; it is not business confirmation or a new
202 acceptance. Access unavailable uses one minimal no-store 404 projection for
unknown, wrong-lineage, expired, revoked or otherwise undisclosable references;
it must not identify which condition applies or claim the booking does not exist.
An unavailable authoritative service returns a minimal 503 projection without a
lineage/state/existence detail, and does not turn prior uncertainty into failure.
Malformed route/query/body input can return a bounded 400 without echoing input;
policy/capacity gates disclose no object facts. Final directional error bodies and
all remaining status/header cases require the approved closed transport profile.

Every response, including denial and service errors, is `application/json` with
`Cache-Control: no-store` and content sniffing disabled. No ETag/Last-Modified or
304 reuse is proposed for this private boundary. CDN, service worker, browser cache,
local/session storage, analytics and restored public page data cannot become a
private status source. No-store alone proves neither privacy nor secure deletion;
permitted in-memory display and legally retained records keep their own rules.

### Reordered replies and truthful recovery

The client binds each request to the selected lineage, current local proof/visit
context and a monotonically replaced request epoch. A route/context change, known
proof loss/revocation or leaving the private process fences old replies, including
errors; aborting a fetch is an optimization, not the fence. No late reply can restore
private controls/data after access loss or switch the selected lineage.

Within that still-current context, a lower committed revision cannot replace a
higher accepted snapshot. Equal revisions with different permitted state/occurrence
content are a protocol inconsistency: do not merge or guess; hold the last permitted
truth with an explicit refresh/recovery indication and bounded fresh-read option.
For equal consistent snapshots, duplicate receipt creates no effect. A matching
newer revision may replace the complete snapshot only after closed shape/calendar/
semantic correlation checks. Proof rotation/loss cannot reset revision handling so
an old response becomes new; it requires the separately approved recovery flow.

Network failure, malformed/truncated reply, timeout, 404 or 503 cannot cancel,
confirm, recreate or resend a booking. Stop private disclosures/actions when access
is unavailable; do not continue showing retained private details as live status.
If proof remains usable but observation fails, label any permitted prior snapshot
as last known, preserve its uncertainty and offer bounded status refresh or the
approved semantic Contact/Book route. Book is not an automatic replacement effect;
unknown prior intent must first be reconciled under its existing lineage authority.

### Primary support and remaining acceptance

Checked 2026-10-07: [RFC 9110 section 9.2.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-9.2.1)
defines safe-method semantics, and [section 15.5.5](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-15.5.5)
permits non-disclosing 404 while making its ordinary cacheability explicit.
[RFC 9111 section 5.2.2.5](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html#section-5.2.2.5)
defines no-store and its privacy limits. [OWASP authorization guidance](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html#validate-the-permissions-on-every-request)
requires per-request permission validation. These support the proposed boundaries;
they do not specify Hengshi's envelope, finite rate, policy or physical mechanisms.

Independent security/architecture review and integrated/founder acceptance remain
required. Freeze the directional response/error and occurrence formats, safe-read
request/resource profile, current-authority/fencing/store mechanisms, class-specific
retention and approved production screens before implementation. Afterwards test
actual HTTP/store/browser boundaries: wrong family/lineage/generation, revocation
versus read/output, missing/present/foreign Origin, private caching/redirects,
provider/alert inactivity under repeated GET, pending state, mixed/equal/lower
revisions, stale errors, context/proof loss and unknown prior operation recovery.
No prose or schema test is added here, and no runtime enforcement is claimed.

Review reference added 2026-10-07: [bounded booking-status read review PASS](reviews/booking-status-read-v1-2026-10-07.md)
covers this additive protocol and eleven exact input identities. The [inspected
contract bytes](../../../output/research/booking-status-read-2026-10-07/PRIVATE_PROCESS_PROOF.md.reviewed)
remain preserved; this later navigation reference is outside them. Exact formats,
finite work limits, physical enforcement, production screens and integrated/founder
acceptance remain held. No runtime result or authorization follows from the receipt.

## Booking status response encoding proposal — 2026-10-07

Status: DOING. Proposed representation at existing IF-BOOK-07 only. The
[response schema](booking-status-response.schema.json) refines the preceding
[read/ordering protocol](#booking-status-read-and-client-ordering-proposal--2026-10-07)
and existing process-field paths. It introduces no client request, new route,
provider authority, cancellation entitlement, identity recovery or production
format acceptance. Earlier reviewed contract bytes are preserved separately.

### Closed successful projection

The complete proposed JSON body has exactly `lineage_id`, `lineage` and `booking`.
`lineage` has exactly `revision` and `state`; `booking` has exactly
`current_occurrence`. References/revisions reuse the named common process value
representations with UUID format assertion. Null is explicit absence of an active
reconciled occurrence at that accepted lifecycle step, not redaction, access loss,
record deletion or an undisclosed successful operation. Omission is invalid.

| Accepted state family | Proposed current_occurrence representation |
|---|---|
| BOOKING_STARTED, VALIDATION_ERROR, QUALIFICATION_COMPLETE, EMAIL_PENDING, EMAIL_EXPIRED, EMAIL_UNDELIVERABLE, VERIFIED, NO_AVAILABILITY, SLOT_SELECTED, BOOKING_PENDING | Required null. A qualification, verified email, offered/selected slot or pending initial provider action cannot create a confirmed occurrence. |
| RECONCILIATION_ERROR | Required null for BF-01's existing initial-submission error branch. A change to an already confirmed occurrence stays in its separately accepted pending-change branch; do not silently remap it here and discard the last reconciled truth. Any different future branch mapping requires a reviewed amendment. |
| CONFIRMED_QUALIFIED, RESCHEDULE_PENDING, CANCEL_PENDING | Required minimal occurrence object from the same committed lineage revision and currently permitted disclosure. Pending changes retain the prior reconciled occurrence while reporting the change as unresolved. Missing/mismatched source truth must not be fabricated to satisfy schema. |
| CANCELLED | Required null for the active occurrence, only after reconciled cancellation. Historical private records retain their separate legal/retention policy; this projection promises neither deletion nor a historical detail endpoint. |

The occurrence object contains exactly `basis: last_reconciled`, `starts_at_utc`
and `ends_at_utc`. The basis labels an observed committed fact, never a fresh
provider query or guarantee that a pending external change has not occurred.
No qualification/email, calendar/meeting/staff/operation identifiers, meeting URL,
proof/CSRF, provider payload, transcript, reason or diagnostics may enter this body.
If current authority cannot disclose a required coherent projection, return the
non-disclosing access/service outcome; do not label redaction as no booking.

Proposed instants use `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ`, exactly 24 ASCII characters, real
calendar/UTC validation and seconds 00–59. Three-digit fractional precision is a
Hengshi representation proposal, not a requirement of RFC 3339. No offset/local
label, leap-second encoding, trimming, padding of an incoming value or implicit
rounding is admitted. The adapter's canonical internal values must already support
lossless serialization and agree with the reconciled record. Unsupported precision
requires approved normalization/adapter semantics; this definition does not guess
them. Preserve the exact UTC instants when displaying visitor-local time with an
unambiguous timezone label under BF-01. Local labels do not alter duration.

The producer's semantic boundary must additionally prove ends > starts and exactly
1,800 elapsed seconds, the complete same-revision/object/owner/provider match,
authority and current lifecycle correspondence before projection. Those checks
cannot be delegated to JSON Schema's lexical/calendar checks. The client validates
the same representation/correlations before accepting a snapshot under the existing
ordering fence; shape alone cannot approve or preserve a booking.

### Closed error pairs and qualification boundary

| Proposed HTTP status | Exact permitted body |
|---|---|
| 400 | `{ "state": "unavailable", "code": "INVALID_REQUEST", "recovery": "correct_request" }` |
| 404 | `{ "state": "unavailable", "code": "ACCESS_UNAVAILABLE", "recovery": "contact" }` |
| 503 | `{ "state": "unavailable", "code": "SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE", "recovery": "refresh_status" }` |

These pairs expose no object existence, selector or branch reason. `contact` names
only the approved semantic route, not a working identity-recovery channel or
response promise. `refresh_status` permits only a bounded read, never provider
retry, resubmission or renewal. The remaining method/media/policy/capacity/header
cases and finite resource/refresh bounds still require their closed transport
profile; these three bodies are not the complete HTTP error surface. Apply the
preceding no-store/no-sniffing/no-redirect rules to successes and errors.

Checked 2026-10-07 against [JSON Schema conditionals](https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/reference/conditionals)
and [format guidance](https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-validation#section-7.2.1).
Calendar/UUID assertion must be explicitly configured; format annotations alone
are insufficient. [RFC 3339 section 5.6](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339.html#section-5.6)
allows other valid timestamp forms that this proposed narrower encoding excludes.
The existing native validator/format-checker fixture is reused without installation
or version selection; no production compatibility conclusion follows from it.

Independent security/architecture review and integrated/founder acceptance remain
required. Validator checks cover closed fields, accepted state/occurrence
correlation, identifiers/revisions and calendar representation only. They cannot
prove duration, raw JSON lexical acceptance, same-revision authority, actual HTTP
status/headers, privacy/store/revocation ordering, provider truth, client fencing
or accessible timezone/recovery behavior. After implementation is authorized,
exercise those actual boundaries and the independently accepted BF-01 scenarios.
No application, public copy, UI, provider/account or proof lifetime is changed.

Review reference added 2026-10-07: [bounded response-shape review PASS](reviews/booking-status-shape-v1-2026-10-07.md)
binds the original 22-input packet and records the verified BKS-01 URL-only
correction separately. This reference is outside those inspected bytes. The
schema/encoding remains proposed; no runtime or integrated acceptance follows.
